{"content_hash": "ea99082ae95a675d", "version_id": 753, "article_id": 76, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Meta gives Zuckerberg new shares to help pay possible tax", "title_zh": "Meta给扎克伯格发新股，帮他应对可能的富豪税", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/22/meta-mark-zuckerberg-california-wealth-tax", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689439518196-f48a24b49fb5?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8bWV0YSUyMHN0cmlrZXMlMjBkZWFsfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTI3OTk4NTF8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Julio Lopez on Unsplash", "author": "Julio Lopez", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@juliolopez?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-person-holding-up-a-cell-phone-in-front-of-a-sign-ilbjfRwOgzA?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(112, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(150, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "ba10886f1e8e"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-24", "word_count": 194, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "Meta has made a deal with its boss Mark Zuckerberg. If California passes a new tax on billionaires, the company will help him pay the bill.", "lead_zh": "Meta和老板马克·扎克伯格达成了一项协议。如果加州通过对亿万富翁征收新税，公司将帮他支付这笔账单。", "preview": "The deal means Zuckerberg will get new shares that he can sell if California passes a one-off 5% wealth tax. In return, he has agreed to sta", "preview_zh": "这项协议意味着，如果加州通过一次性5%的富豪税，扎克伯格将获得可以出售的新股票。作为交换，他同意在未来八年内继续住在加州，或Meta总部所在地。他的身家为2390亿美元。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 741, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 80.1, "size_bytes": 481536, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 231, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 81.75, "size_bytes": 491472, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 231, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 88.35, "size_bytes": 531072, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 231, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 76.5, "size_bytes": 459936, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 231, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 81.775, "size_bytes": 491616, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 231, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fec3522/content/data/versions/753.json", "paragraphs": ["The deal means Zuckerberg will get new shares that he can sell if California passes a one-off 5% wealth tax. In return, he has agreed to stay a resident of California, or wherever Meta has its base, for eight years. Zuckerberg is worth $239bn.", "Californians will vote next month on Proposition 40, which would tax about 250 billionaires in the state. Zuckerberg told Meta he was thinking about moving because the tax could force him to sell voting shares. Meta is creating a new class of non-voting shares so he can sell some without losing control.", "Recent polling shows Prop 40 still lacks majority support, and tech billionaires are spending heavily to fight it. However, Meta also reported a 26% rise in revenue to $64.6bn, although profits fell 37% to $13bn because of a $9.9bn charge over child protection and addiction cases.", "The company's shares fell more than 6% on Thursday, which helped pull the Nasdaq index down 2.5%. In a separate case, a New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25bn because it misled the public about Facebook user data. Meta also cut its headcount to 66,775, 15% fewer than a year ago."], "paragraphs_zh": ["这项协议意味着，如果加州通过一次性5%的富豪税，扎克伯格将获得可以出售的新股票。作为交换，他同意在未来八年内继续住在加州，或Meta总部所在地。他的身家为2390亿美元。", "加州人下个月将就第40号提案投票，该提案将向该州约250名亿万富翁征税。扎克伯格告诉Meta，他正在考虑搬走，因为这项税可能迫使他卖掉有投票权的股票。Meta正在设立一种新的无投票权股票，这样他就能卖掉一部分而不会失去控制权。", "近期民调显示，第40号提案仍未获得多数支持，科技富豪们正花大钱反对它。不过，Meta也公布收入增长26%，达到646亿美元，但利润因儿童保护和成瘾案件相关的99亿美元费用下降37%，至130亿美元。", "公司股价周四下跌超过6%，拖累纳斯达克指数下跌2.5%。在另一起案件中，新墨西哥州一名法官命令Meta支付250亿美元，因为它在Facebook用户数据问题上误导了公众。Meta还披露员工人数降至66775人，比一年前减少15%。"], "body": "The deal means Zuckerberg will get new shares that he can sell if California passes a one-off 5% wealth tax. In return, he has agreed to stay a resident of California, or wherever Meta has its base, for eight years. Zuckerberg is worth $239bn.\n\nCalifornians will vote next month on Proposition 40, which would tax about 250 billionaires in the state. Zuckerberg told Meta he was thinking about moving because the tax could force him to sell voting shares. Meta is creating a new class of non-voting shares so he can sell some without losing control.\n\nRecent polling shows Prop 40 still lacks majority support, and tech billionaires are spending heavily to fight it. However, Meta also reported a 26% rise in revenue to $64.6bn, although profits fell 37% to $13bn because of a $9.9bn charge over child protection and addiction cases.\n\nThe company's shares fell more than 6% on Thursday, which helped pull the Nasdaq index down 2.5%. In a separate case, a New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25bn because it misled the public about Facebook user data. Meta also cut its headcount to 66,775, 15% fewer than a year ago.", "body_zh": "这项协议意味着，如果加州通过一次性5%的富豪税，扎克伯格将获得可以出售的新股票。作为交换，他同意在未来八年内继续住在加州，或Meta总部所在地。他的身家为2390亿美元。\n\n加州人下个月将就第40号提案投票，该提案将向该州约250名亿万富翁征税。扎克伯格告诉Meta，他正在考虑搬走，因为这项税可能迫使他卖掉有投票权的股票。Meta正在设立一种新的无投票权股票，这样他就能卖掉一部分而不会失去控制权。\n\n近期民调显示，第40号提案仍未获得多数支持，科技富豪们正花大钱反对它。不过，Meta也公布收入增长26%，达到646亿美元，但利润因儿童保护和成瘾案件相关的99亿美元费用下降37%，至130亿美元。\n\n公司股价周四下跌超过6%，拖累纳斯达克指数下跌2.5%。在另一起案件中，新墨西哥州一名法官命令Meta支付250亿美元，因为它在Facebook用户数据问题上误导了公众。Meta还披露员工人数降至66775人，比一年前减少15%。", "text": "The deal means Zuckerberg will get new shares that he can sell if California passes a one-off 5% wealth tax. In return, he has agreed to stay a resident of California, or wherever Meta has its base, for eight years. Zuckerberg is worth $239bn. Californians will vote next month on Proposition 40, which would tax about 250 billionaires in the state. Zuckerberg told Meta he was thinking about moving because the tax could force him to sell voting shares. Meta is creating a new class of non-voting shares so he can sell some without losing control. Recent polling shows Prop 40 still lacks majority support, and tech billionaires are spending heavily to fight it. However, Meta also reported a 26% rise in revenue to $64.6bn, although profits fell 37% to $13bn because of a $9.9bn charge over child protection and addiction cases. The company's shares fell more than 6% on Thursday, which helped pull the Nasdaq index down 2.5%. In a separate case, a New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25bn because it misled the public about Facebook user data. Meta also cut its headcount to 66,775, 15% fewer than a year ago.", "vocab": [{"word": "strike a deal", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "达成协议", "note": "常与with连用：strike a deal with sb", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "one-off", "pos": "adj", "zh": "一次性的", "note": "指只发生一次的税或付款", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "wealth tax", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "财富税、富豪税", "note": "按资产而非收入征税", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "resident", "pos": "noun", "zh": "居民", "note": "be a resident of + 地点", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "vote on", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "就……投票", "note": "vote on a proposal", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "polling", "pos": "noun", "zh": "民调", "note": "polling shows that...", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "majority support", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "多数支持", "note": "lack majority support 缺乏多数支持", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "revenue", "pos": "noun", "zh": "收入、营收", "note": "公司营收常用复数 revenues", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "mislead", "pos": "verb", "zh": "误导", "note": "过去式 misled", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "headcount", "pos": "noun", "zh": "员工人数", "note": "cut headcount 裁减员工", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-10-23T23:57:30.310630", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.388, "sm": 275, "em": 387, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "deal", "s": 0.388, "e": 0.65, "sm": 387, "em": 650, "cs": 4, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "means", "s": 0.65, "e": 0.988, "sm": 650, "em": 987, "cs": 9, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "Zuckerberg", "s": 0.988, "e": 1.538, "sm": 987, "em": 1537, "cs": 15, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "will", "s": 1.538, "e": 1.65, "sm": 1537, "em": 1649, "cs": 26, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "get", "s": 1.65, "e": 1.862, "sm": 1650, "em": 1862, "cs": 31, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "new", "s": 1.863, "e": 2.062, "sm": 1862, "em": 2062, "cs": 35, "ce": 38, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "shares", "s": 2.062, "e": 2.525, "sm": 2062, "em": 2524, "cs": 39, "ce": 45, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "that", "s": 2.525, "e": 2.637, "sm": 2525, "em": 2637, "cs": 46, "ce": 50, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "he", "s": 2.638, "e": 2.725, "sm": 2637, "em": 2724, "cs": 51, "ce": 53, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "can", "s": 2.725, "e": 2.913, "sm": 2725, "em": 2912, "cs": 54, "ce": 57, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "sell", "s": 2.913, "e": 3.225, "sm": 2912, "em": 3225, "cs": 58, "ce": 